# ASP.NET Core Example

Suppose we have this interface.

```csharp
public interface IUserService
{
    User GetById(int id);

    void Add(User user);

    void Update(User user);

    void Delete(int id);
}
```

Instead, split it.

Read

```csharp
public interface IUserReader
{
    User GetById(int id);
}
```

Write

```csharp
public interface IUserWriter
{
    void Add(User user);

    void Update(User user);
}
```

Delete

```csharp
public interface IUserDeleter
{
    void Delete(int id);
}
```

Benefits

- Read-only APIs depend only on IUserReader.
- Admin APIs depend on all interfaces.
- Better dependency injection.
- Easier unit testing.

